        explanation: "Choral and vocal music existed for centuries, but the symphony — since Haydn — had been defined as a purely instrumental genre. By breaking that wall in the finale of the Ninth, Beethoven forced every subsequent symphonist (Brahms, Mahler, Bruckner, Shostakovich) to take a position for or against choral symphonies. The Ninth literally redefined the form.",
